<title>JAPAN: Japan Aug soybean imports down 20.4 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan Aug soybean imports down 20.4 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's soybean imports in August totalled 307,617 tonnes, down by 20.4 percent from a year ago, according to Finance Ministry data released on Monday.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Aug 96	  July 96	Aug 95</p>
<p> Total imports    307,617	 445,079	386,442</p>
<p>Major suppliers of soybeans (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		 256,388	 311,028	295,354</p>
<p> Brazil		43,023	  94,522	 64,061</p>
<p> Paraguay	     6,000	  25,781	 16,798</p>
<p> China		    521	   9,895	  6,548</p>
<p>Imports in the first eight months of 1996 were 3,300,805 tonnes against 3,300,961 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
</text>
